 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair came in at 33% of normal on the middle of the grids, and January to February sat at 24%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 184% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 27159 had its driest year in 1988, at 59% of normal.</p>"}
